<title>CHINA: S.CHINA BROKERAGE H1 NET JUMPS 293 PCT.</title>
<headline>S.CHINA BROKERAGE H1 NET JUMPS 293 PCT.</headline>
<dateline>HONG KONG 1997-08-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>Six months ended June 30</p>
<p>(in million HK$ unless stated)</p>
<p>    Shr (H.K. cents)	   2.23   vs 0.58 (see note)</p>
<p>    Dividend (H.K. cents)    0.4    vs 0.375 (see note)</p>
<p>    Exceptional items	  nil    vs nil</p>
<p>    Net			    72.88  vs 18.53</p>
<p>    Turnover		     191.02 vs 88.99</p>
<p>    Company name		 South China Brokerage Co Ltd</p>
<p>    Books close		  September 18-19</p>
<p>    Dividend payable	   September 26</p>
<p>NOTE - South China Brokerage is a financial services company.</p>
<p>The company proposed a bonus issue one warrant for every five shares and one-for-five shares held.</p>
<p>On May 17, 1997 every issued and unissued share of HK$0.1 each in the capital of the company was subdivided into four subdivided shares of HK$0.025 each. A bonus issue of subdivided shares on the basis of one bonus subdivided shares for every subdivided share was also made on the same date. Therefore, the calculation of earnings per share and interim dividend for the period ended June 30, 1997, and the corresponding period were adjusted accordingly.</p>
<p>-- Hong Kong News Room (852) 2843 6368</p>
